WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.405
Week 35: Analysis, Argument, and Professional Listening. identify main idea and supporting detail defend an opinion summarize unfamiliar material

2
00:00:10.405 --> 00:00:25.505
Form and meaning. Applying the form. Build formal arguments with sequencing connectors (en primer/segundo lugar) and contrast connectors (por un lado/por otro lado), then support each claim with sostener que + evidence.

3
00:00:25.505 --> 00:00:51.465
Model set. Por un lado, hay beneficios claros. Por otro lado, existen riesgos. En primer lugar, revisamos los datos. Sostengo que la propuesta es sólida. Alguien podría refutar este punto. On one hand, there are clear benefits. On the other hand, there are risks. In the first place, we reviewed the data. I maintain that the proposal is solid. Someone could refute this point.

4
00:00:51.465 --> 00:01:01.595
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:01:01.595 --> 00:01:15.799
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: identify main idea and supporting detail; defend an opinion; summarize unfamiliar material. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:15.799 --> 00:01:42.740
Model language. Por un lado, hay beneficios claros. — On one hand, there are clear benefits. Por otro lado, existen riesgos. — On the other hand, there are risks. En primer lugar, revisamos los datos. — In the first place, we reviewed the data. Sostengo que la propuesta es sólida. — I maintain that the proposal is solid. Alguien podría refutar este punto. — Someone could refute this point.

7
00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:52.489
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
